A Fluent scrollbar's thumb, on Linux and Windows, is one solid colour quad clipped to a rounded rect
of its own. That clip needs no render surface, but its shared quad state wasn't marked a fast
rounded corner, and viz merges a surface into its embedding quad's pass only when every rounded mask
in it is fast and fits inside the embedder's. So any scrollable page shown under fast rounded
corners, as the core's panes are on Linux (core/platform/linux/window_views.cc), was drawn into a
render pass of its own each frame and then copied, its thumb's mask the one thing keeping it from
merging (#2377). By its source, Chrome's own page pays the same in its split view and wherever its
contents are rounded, as NativeViewHostAura gives the page's layer fast rounded corners there. The
flag is read only by the aggregator's merge test, so the thumb draws as before, with its own mask.
--- a/cc/layers/painted_scrollbar_layer_impl.cc
+++ b/cc/layers/painted_scrollbar_layer_impl.cc
@@ -144,6 +144,10 @@
           gfx::RRectF(gfx::RectF(thumb_quad_rect), rounded_corner_radius));
       shared_quad_state->mask_filter_info.ApplyTransform(
           draw_properties().target_space_transform);
+      // The mask clips the thumb's one quad and needs no render surface, so
+      // viz can merge a surface showing it into an embedding quad's pass that
+      // has fast rounded corners of its own.
+      shared_quad_state->is_fast_rounded_corner = true;
     }
     auto* thumb_quad =
         render_pass->CreateAndAppendDrawQuad<viz::SolidColorDrawQuad>();
